    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [ ] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version (irrelevant, I think? -- not using mini.nvim)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nechasnovski/mini.move\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThe separate git repo does not have a `stable` branch.\r\n\r\nI can install from the default branch just fine, but the README says I stable branch should exist?\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.9.0-dev-629+gd89290b45\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. check github branches on repo: https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.move\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nstable branch exists\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nstable branch does not exist",
